.TH recipe-manuals 7 "Lentil Tacos" "" "Lentil Tacos"

.SH NAME
Lentil Tacos

.SH INGREDIENTS
.IP \[bu]
Lentils, Cooked (125mL, 1/2 cup)
.IP \[bu]
Red Onion (half, finely diced)
.IP \[bu]
Jalapeño (2, finely diced)
.IP \[bu]
Tomato (half, finely diced)
.IP \[bu]
Garlic (2 cloves, minced)
.IP \[bu]
Vegetable Broth (62.5mL, 1/4 cup)
.IP \[bu]
Olive Oil (30mL, 2 tablespoons)
.IP \[bu]
Sriracha (5mL, 1 teaspoon)
.IP \[bu]
Taco Seasoning (15mL, 1 tablespoon)
.IP \[bu]
Taco Shells

.SH INSTRUCTIONS
.nr step 1 1
.IP \n[step]
In a pan, combine \fBred onion\fR (half, finely diced), \fBjalapeño\fR (2,
finely diced), \fBtomato\fR (half, finely diced), \fBgarlic\fR (2 cloves,
minced), \fBolive oil\fR (30ml, 2 tablespoons). Cook at medium heat for
10 minutes.
.IP \n+[step]
Add \fBvegetable broth\fR (62.5ml, 1/4 cup), \fBtaco seasoning\fR (15ml, 1
tablespoon), \fBlentils, cooked\fR (125ml, 1/2 cup) and cook until liquid
has evaporated, approximately 3 minutes.
.IP \n+[step]
Serve, garnishing with toppings of choice.

.SH COMMENT
.IP \[bu]
Estimated Prep Time: 10m
.IP \[bu]
Estimated Cook Time: 30m
.IP \[bu]
Difficulty: Easy

.SH ADDITIONAL NOTES
Serving with a hard shell wrapped in a soft tortilla is pleasant and not
as messy.

Corn, cheese and salsa are great for garnishing. Pico de gallo or a home
made sweet salsa can take the recipe to another level.

Not all taco seasonings are created equal. It's a good idea to taste
and adjust salt levels if needed.
